# Pillow Thief mobile app environment (copy to .env — never commit real values)
# ==========================================
# Day-to-day development runs in Expo Go. The app uses Expo Router for
# navigation, Supabase for the backend (auth, bookings, payments) and
# react-native-maps for the map surfaces.
#
# Required, always:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL        your Supabase project URL
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   your anon / publishable key
#
# Google Maps tiles require a DEVELOPMENT BUILD. Nothing in this file can make
# Google Maps render inside Expo Go — see "Maps" below.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Copy this file to apps/mobile/.env
#   2. Fill in the two EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_* values
#   3. cd apps/mobile && npm install && npx expo start
#   4. Open Expo Go and scan the QR (or enter exp://<your-lan-ip>:8081)
# ==========================================

# Supabase project (local dev: values from `supabase start`)
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# --- Maps -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Native Google Maps keys. app.config.ts reads these at BUILD time and writes
# them into the AndroidManifest / Info.plist, so they need a native rebuild.
#
# They do NOT work in Expo Go. Expo Go stopped shipping a usable Google Maps key
# in SDK 52, so on Android the map is blank no matter which key you set. What
# you actually get per platform:
#
#   Expo Go + iOS      -> Apple Maps renders, no key needed.
#   Expo Go + Android  -> no tiles. The Explore Map screen shows the provider
#                         list and an accurate notice instead of a grey box.
#   dev build + key    -> Google Maps tiles on both platforms.
#
# For real tiles on Android, set the key below and run:
#   cd apps/mobile && npx expo run:android
#
# Restrict the key to package app.pillowthief.mobile plus your signing SHA-1.
# Full steps: docs/GOOGLE_MAPS.md
# GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_KEY=AIza...
# GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_KEY=AIza...

# Shows the simulated-payment banner in dev. This affects PAYMENTS ONLY — it has
# no effect on map behaviour.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SANDBOX_MODE=true
